{"kind":"assert","text":"PB-3, on checker findings e6f2b242 and the revised head 342de7a3 (gate START 1cf9c7f8): both choices are approved.\n1. When the own row expires while the view is open, the client emits `expired` and re-enters only on the next set() or an explicit call. With renewal off, an idle member leaves the room view after one lease. That is honest and costs nothing. Automatic renewal arrives with the LL-1 source head and keeps an idle member present.\n2. The caller wires pagehide to close(). The note must say that a leave sent from pagehide may not reach the room before the page unloads, and that the lease timer then removes the row within one lease. A keepalive or beacon leave is a later improvement, not part of PB-3.\nAfter a passing gate at 342de7a3, request the checker's review of that exact head. I land it and deploy.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}